From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: verify board-specific RTL826x SDS mode

Keep the upstream board property and RTK SerDes recovery sequence. Check
that the host SDS mode survives the write, propagating read errors and
rejecting mismatches instead of reporting a successfully configured PHY.
The generic RTL826x patch already exposes the SDS accessor helpers.
Document the existing optional property in the device tree binding.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/realtek,rtl82xx.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/realtek,rtl82xx.yaml
@@ -50,6 +50,13 @@
     description:
       Enable ALDPS mode, ALDPS mode default is disabled after hardware reset.
 
+  realtek,sds-mode:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+    maximum: 65535
+    description: |
+      Board-specific 16-bit host SerDes mode programmed into SDS page 6,
+      register 3 after the RTL825x/RTL826x firmware initialization sequence.
+
   wakeup-source:
     type: boolean
     description:
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -3269,7 +3269,7 @@
 {
 	struct device *dev = &phydev->mdio.dev;
 	u32 mode;
-	int ret;
+	int readback, ret;
 
 	if (!device_property_present(dev, "realtek,sds-mode"))
 		return 0;
@@ -3290,6 +3290,22 @@
 	if (ret) {
 		phydev_err(phydev, "failed to set SDS mode 0x%04x: %d\n", mode, ret);
 		return ret;
+	}
+
+	readback = rtl826x_phy_patch_sds_get(phydev,
+					     RTL826X_SDS_HOST_MODE_PAGE,
+					     RTL826X_SDS_HOST_MODE_REG);
+	if (readback < 0) {
+		phydev_err(phydev, "failed to read back SDS mode: %d\n",
+			   readback);
+		return readback;
+	}
+
+	if (readback != mode) {
+		phydev_err(phydev,
+			   "SDS mode readback mismatch: wrote 0x%04x, read 0x%04x\n",
+			   mode, readback);
+		return -EIO;
 	}
 
 	phydev_info(phydev, "configured SDS mode 0x%04x\n", mode);
